        "source_text_reference": "MANAGEMENT AT DISTRICT HOSPITAL\n• Admit and re-assess\n• Optimise therapy with furosemide/ARNI/\nspironolactone/ O2 and stabilize\n• Consider non-invasive ventilation if marked respiratory\ndistress and O2 saturation < 90%\n• Echocardiography:  conﬁrm diagnosis of HFrEF: LV\nejection fraction < 35%\n• Search for etiological diagnosis\n• Consider β  blockers after decongestion\n• Refer back to CHC/ PHC after stabilization",
