          "cells": {
            "Smoking Salt Physical Weight Moderation Co Cessation restriction activity Reduction of alcohol": "FUROSEMIDE • Dose 20-80 mg daily PO • Intravenous 10-80 mg SOS in acute stage • Change to oral when symptoms subside • Monitor serum electrolytes, creatinine and uric acid on therapy",
            "Column_2": "",
            "Column_3": "• CARVEDILOL Dose 3.125 to 25 mg twice daily PO METOPROLOL 12.5-50mg twice daily PO BISOPROLOL 1.25-10mg once a day PO PRECAUTIONS • Start after decongestion with low dose with BP > 100 mmHg and HR >60/min • Uptitrate dose 1-2 weekly till maximum tolerable dose • Keep watch on BP, heart rate and recipitation of CHF symptoms • Increase diuretics and reduce carvedilol to manage reappearance of CHF",
            "Column_4": "",
            "ntrol of DM HTN/ Lipids": "",
            "/": "ARNI • Dose 50 to 200 mg twice daily PO • Start with low dose with BP >100 mmHg, normal electrolyte and creatinine less than 2.5 mg/dl • Uptitrate dose 1-2 weekly till maximum tolerable dose • Keep watch on BP and electrolytes before every increment and on follow-up",
            "Secondary CVD prevention with aspirin and statins": "",
            "Column_8": "",
            "Column_9": ""
